    "result_text": "The only test class is `AcceptanceTest`, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe create audit line now also logs `membershipLevel` and `membershipNumber`, keeping all previously logged fields.\n\nI made a single, minimal change in `SaveOwner.java` (the only class that emits the create AUDIT line):\n\n- Extended the log format string with `membershipLevel={} membershipNumber={}`.\n- Computed the values by reusing the existing helpers already used by `OwnerMapper` \u2014 `MembershipTier.level(MembershipTier.points(...))` and `MembershipNumber.of(...)` \u2014 from the owner's own fields (`namesakeCount`, `email`, `registrationDate`, `customerCode`).\n\nThis keeps structural impact low: one file touched, one function changed (`service`, CC=1, no sibling methods so `WMC_other`=1), and no new classes or complexity introduced. Verified against the sample audit output:\n\n```\nAUDIT - Created owner id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E registrationDate=2026-09-07 membershipLevel=2 membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M26\n```\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
